      "title": "revert: \"SocketCAN: Treat non-CAN-XL packets with length > 16 bytes as CAN-FD\"",
      "message": "revert: \"SocketCAN: Treat non-CAN-XL packets with length > 16 bytes as CAN-FD\"\n\nThis reverts commit d48366c9f9e2f395aa9d3768184f9bcd8cef8b77\n\nIn the reverted commit the length of the CAN frame data is used to\ndistinguish CAN CC frames from CAN FD frames to apparently 'fix' a\ndefective generated capture file.\nThere is no way to separate CAN CC/FD frames through their length\ninformation and therefore this patch added a wrong heuristic instead\nof dropping and/or notifying the broken capture file content.\n\nSee discussion about the merge request:\nhttps://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/merge_requests/18710\n\nThis patch squashed the three commits from merge request:\nhttps://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/merge_requests/18831\n\nCC: Giovanni Musto <giovanni.musto@partner.italdesign.it>\nCC: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>\nCC: Guy Harris <gharris@sonic.net>\nSigned-off-by: Oliver Hartkopp <socketcan@hartkopp.net>\n",
